ROCm 7.1.0's LLVM (ROCm/llvm-project 1b0eada6): CodeGenPrepare compile time, from upstream LLVM
e80f32fd20bf, "[CodeGenPrepare] Use Instruction::comesBefore instead of manual ordering" (#190485).

tryToSinkFreeOperands numbered every instruction of its basic block, in a DenseMap built anew for each
instruction it looked at, which is quadratic in the length of the block. Instruction::comesBefore
gives the same order (upstream: "the exact same ordering"), so the generated code does not change.
ROCm 7.1 predates upstream's other change to this loop (the side-effect and memory checks beside
isa<PHINode>), which this backport leaves out.

--- a/llvm/lib/CodeGen/CodeGenPrepare.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/CodeGen/CodeGenPrepare.cpp
@@ -7648,17 +7648,12 @@ bool CodeGenPrepare::tryToSinkFreeOperands(Instruction *I) {
   bool Changed = false;
   SmallVector<Use *, 4> ToReplace;
   Instruction *InsertPoint = I;
-  DenseMap<const Instruction *, unsigned long> InstOrdering;
-  unsigned long InstNumber = 0;
-  for (const auto &I : *TargetBB)
-    InstOrdering[&I] = InstNumber++;
-
   for (Use *U : reverse(OpsToSink)) {
     auto *UI = cast<Instruction>(U->get());
     if (isa<PHINode>(UI))
       continue;
     if (UI->getParent() == TargetBB) {
-      if (InstOrdering[UI] < InstOrdering[InsertPoint])
+      if (UI->comesBefore(InsertPoint))
         InsertPoint = UI;
       continue;
     }
